From 23520c6f2ed41c40a288a01536b02a95bcd521d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 01:48:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Hide the map edge with a ring of far hills and mountains
 (#885)

The backdrop's ground was a rectangle whose edge showed when the camera
zoomed out or tilted up. The ground is now an ellipse ringed by far hills,
with lavender mountains (the sky's haze colour) behind them, tall enough to
hide the edge at the 40 stud zoom cap and with it off. The open ground gets
fields with crop rows and hedges, copses and up to three ponds. Works for
Backdrop, BackdropBig and BackdropWide; nothing collides or casts shadows.

Backdrop 21496 tris, 696 parts; Big 21244 / 698; Wide 23232 / 767. All PASS,
z-fight 0. Sheet: docs/concepts/clean-a-cat/2026-11-27-map-edge-885.jpg

Part of #885

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DW2up1ahn23P9Rf5xanBXQ
